{"seconds": 235.5, "exit": 0, "final": "**Best move:** Be5+\n\n**Main line:** Be5+ Kd5 Bxc3 Re5+ Bdxe5\n\n**Motif:** Deflection\n\n**Coaching note (77 words):**\n\nWhen a piece is defended only by the king, look for a forcing move\u2014especially a check\u2014that drives the king away. Here, **Be5+** forces the king to move and abandons the c3 rook's defense. Then **Bxc3** wins a whole rook! This \"deflection\" tactic works whenever: (1) only the king defends, (2) you have a forcing move, and (3) capturing that piece wins material. Whenever you spot a king defending something, ask yourself: \"How can I lure the king away?\" Forcing moves like checks are your answer.\n\n```json\n{\"move\": \"Be5+\", \"line\": [\"Be5+\", \"Kd5\", \"Bxc3\", \"Re5+\", \"Bdxe5\"], \"motifs\": [\"deflection\"]}\n```", "tool_calls": [{"tool": "skill", "args": {"skill": "chess-coach"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-board", "args": {"fen": "8/2p5/3b4/pp4k1/3KR1P1/1PR4r/8/8 b - - 3 38"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-threats", "args": {"fen": "8/2p5/3b4/pp4k1/3KR1P1/1PR4r/8/8 b - - 3 38"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-legal_moves", "args": {"fen": "8/2p5/3b4/pp4k1/3KR1P1/1PR4r/8/8 b - - 3 38"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "8/2p5/3b4/pp4k1/3KR1P1/1PR4r/8/8 b - - 3 38", "move": "Rd3"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "8/2p5/3b4/pp4k1/3KR1P1/1PRr4/8/8 w - - 4 39", "move": "Kxd3"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "8/2p5/3b4/pp4k1/3KR1P1/1PRr4/8/8 w - - 4 39", "move": "Rxd3"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "8/2p5/3b4/pp4k1/3KR1P1/1PR4r/8/8 b - - 3 38", "move": "c5"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "8/2p5/3b4/pp4k1/3KR1P1/1PR4r/8/8 b - - 3 38", "move": "Rxc3"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-legal_moves", "args": {"fen": "8/2p5/3b4/pp4k1/3KR1P1/1PRr4/8/8 w - - 4 39"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-legal_moves", "args": {"fen": "8/2p5/3b4/pp4k1/4R1P1/1PRK4/8/8 b - - 0 39"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "8